WEBVTT

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:16.930
<i>Although we're all very worried</i>
<i>about Mokichi's condition,</i>

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.060
<i>the fourth game is starting soon!</i>

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.930
SAYAKA KATAHARA
DAUGHTER OF METSUDO KATAHARA

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.190
RESERVED FOR OHMA TOKITA
YAMASHITA CORPORATION

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.610
You look pretty good
in the shorts I gave you.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.690
OHMA TOKITA
FIGHTER, YAMASHITA CORPORATION

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.740
You'll be called soon, Ohma.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.700
KAEDE AKIYAMA
CHAIRMAN'S SECRETARY, NOGI GROUP

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.410
-Okay, I'm off now.
-Um... Ohma.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.410
KAZUO YAMASHITA
PRESIDENT, YAMASHITA CORP.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.950
I know I shouldn't be saying
this to you right before your match,

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.460
but if you ever feel your life is in
danger, you must withdraw from the game.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:51.380
Your life... is much more important
to me than money.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.430
Kazuo Yamashita.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.350
-Stop interfering.
-You think I'm interfering?

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.060
-I'm just worried about--
-I won't lose.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.770
Think about how you're going
to reward me when I win.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.740
SUKIZO URITA
PRESIDENT, PENASONIC CORPORATION

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:22.910
It's been a while since I've
seen you walk on two legs.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.620
Inaba.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.380
I badly want to win this tournament.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.420
-I'm counting on you.
-Got it!

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.880
RYO INABA
FIGHTER, PENASONIC CORPORATION

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.430
Well, we'd better get going, too.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.180
Hi, Mr. Yamashita.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:46.180
You're, um... Mr. Urita,
the president of Penasonic Corporation.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.860
-Is there something I can do for you?
-I have a proposal.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.070
How about a bet, just
between the two of us?

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.650
Did you say... a bet?

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:01.870
Private betting between individuals
is not one of the prohibited activities.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.240
She's right.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.120
I just thought we could have a little fun.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.580
-Hmm.
-I'll bet...

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:13.090
ten TVs from our company.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:17.050
-Ten TVs!
-That sounds great!

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:21.010
To be honest,
I've been wanting to get a Penasonic TV.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.140
<i>Has he been waiting for this opportunity?</i>

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.850
Okay, Mr. Yamashita.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.100
Then, what are you
prepared to bet in return?

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:34.110
Let me see...

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:39.740
If I lose, I'll give you the equivalent
to what the TVs are worth.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:44.240
-What do you say?
-That's fine. It's a bet.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:48.870
<i>I proposed the bet to see</i>
<i>the caliber of the man.</i>

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.880
<i>I didn't expect him</i>
<i>to accept it so easily.</i>

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.590
-That was very stupid.
-It's not a problem.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:01.130
It's only ten TVs. It's peanuts
compared to what I already owe.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.930
He was using
Kengan Association code words.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.970
When someone offers
a product from "our company",

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.730
they mean shares in that company.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:11.310
Shares?

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:16.780
And the number means the percentage.
Which means...

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:21.740
you've just accepted a high stakes gamble
betting ten percent of Penasonic's shares.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:23.910
<i>What? No!</i>

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.580
<i>Penasonic Corporation is</i>
<i>the biggest electronics company in Japan,</i>

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:30.910
<i>and he's betting</i>
<i>ten percent of their shares?</i>

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:35.340
By the way, based on Penasonic
Corporation's current stock price,

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:38.590
the amount you'd pay
if you lose is about...

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.170
Two hundred and eighty billion yen.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:18.900
ASHURA

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:27.160
Let us present the man who is going
to whip up a storm in the kengan field.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:30.160
<i>He was the driving force behind</i>
<i>this tournament.</i>

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.330
GAME FOUR

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:35.330
<i>He's finally making his grand entrance.</i>

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.580
<i>His background is completely unknown.</i>

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:43.670
<i>This mysterious new fighter promises</i>
<i>to be a sensation in the tournament.</i>

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:48.550
<i>Standing 182 cm tall and weighing 85 kg,</i>

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:52.180
<i>his kengan match record is</i>
<i>two wins and no losses.</i>

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:58.100
He has acquired total assets
of 154 billion, 230 million yen.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:02.020
Representing Yamashita Corporation,
also known as "The Ashura,"

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:06.030
<i>Ohma Tokita!</i>

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.450
SETSUNA KIRYU
FIGHTER, KOUOU EDUCATION GROUP

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:16.450
Ohma, my love!

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.870
You look perfectly prepared.
I want you so much right now!

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.920
TOMOKO MATSUDA
CHAIRWOMAN'S SECRETARY, KOUOU EDU.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.460
<i>He's a menacing assassin monster.</i>

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:28.340
<i>His appearance has been much-anticipated.</i>

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:31.510
<i>Penasonic Corporation,</i>
<i>unbeaten in six years,</i>

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:35.270
<i>has sent a new thug to the tournament.</i>

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.270
<i>His only desire is to be the champion.</i>

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:42.520
<i>Standing 155 cm tall and weighing 62 kg,</i>

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:45.860
<i>he makes his kengan match debut today.</i>

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:51.110
Representing Penasonic Corporation,
also known as "The Black Phantom,"

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:54.950
<i>Ryo Inaba!</i>

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:03.040
Huh?

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:08.170
No!

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.260
KEIZABURO SAWADA
FIGHTER, MURDER MUSIC

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:12.510
He's so creepy looking.
He's definitely not my type.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:14.010
What would you do if he were?

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:15.720
YOSHIKO TOGAWA
PRESIDENT, MURDER MUSIC

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:22.480
<i>He's small.</i>

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.650
<i>But that means nothing.</i>

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.740
<i>I know what he is, the way I always know.</i>

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:32.410
<i>Not by anything cheap like logic,</i>
<i>but by intuition...</i>

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:36.490
<i>This jerk is strong.</i>

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.620
Take your stance!

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.130
Fight!

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:07.610
<i>This is a fierce exchange of blows!</i>

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:10.360
<i>It's been an even match so far.</i>

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.360
No, she's wrong.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.370
Ohma is superior.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:21.750
This is his chance!

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:23.500
Go Ohma!

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:35.220
<i>His movement is...</i>

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:38.350
Shit!

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:47.940
Look! Inaba's moves have changed.

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:59.990
Inaba's tactics seem
to be working effectively.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.040
<i>With a hit-and-retreat strategy,</i>

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:05.580
<i>he's trying to slowly but surely</i>
<i>wear Ohma out.</i>

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:07.710
Okay, keep going.

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:14.840
<i>Ohma looks frustrated</i>
<i>at not getting a chance to attack.</i>

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:17.140
<i>He can't seem to hide his irritation.</i>

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:19.850
COSMO IMAI & AKIRA NISHIHONJI
NISHIHONJI SECURITY SERVICES

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:22.520
That's a unique technique
in the Inaba Style, called Edging.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:23.930
Have you seen it before, Akira?

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.980
Yeah, it looks similar to shuffling,

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:31.610
but what makes it unique is that
they move only by using their toes.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.490
<i>Whoa! Ohma hit him!</i>

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:44.790
<i>I see.</i>

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.870
<i>Ohma was measuring intervals</i>
<i>by clicking his tongue.</i>

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:52.960
<i>Inaba tried to confuse Ohma by changing</i>
<i>the length and speed of his steps.</i>

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:56.420
<i>But unfortunately for you, your</i>
<i>opponent isn't so easy to fool, Inaba.</i>

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:00.010
<i>Your style won't work</i>
<i>against the Niko Style.</i>

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:01.640
NIKO STYLE - FLAME KATA: FLASHFIRE!

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:04.720
You might want to try
a different trick now.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:08.600
That won't work anymore.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:13.110
Oh, you're going back to
what you used to be like,

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:15.110
my darling Ohma Tokita.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:20.370
Great! Ohma's got his momentum back.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.500
What's wrong, <i>kombu </i>boy?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.290
Is the sideshow over?

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:33.500
<i>Got him!</i>

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:39.930
<i>Whoa, what's happening over there?</i>

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.850
<i>Why did he stop?</i>

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:46.020
What? It's his hair!

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:52.400
<i>Inaba's hair is wrapped around Ohma's leg!</i>

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:54.770
It's "Spider's Hair", in the Inaba Style.

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:57.900
This is your first experience
fighting hair, isn't it?

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.410
<i>Ohma Tokita.</i>

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:12.880
Time to switch offense and defense.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:15.880
Oh, gosh! He's so cute!

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.460
Switch what?

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:21.840
I have no desire at all
to shift to defense.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:27.140
Were you going to tear my hair out?

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.390
It's impossible.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:31.900
<i>His hair has thrown Tokita into the air!</i>

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:34.400
NIKO STYLE - ADAMANTINE KATA:
INDESTRUCTIBLE

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:39.990
<i>I knew the Adamantine Kata</i>
<i>wasn't my thing.</i>

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.910
<i>I didn't tighten my muscles enough.</i>

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.540
I'm going to punish you.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.250
<i>That hair is no ordinary hair.</i>

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:55.670
<i>It's a chain!</i>

00:11:57.170 --> 00:12:01.630
<i>Hair is the strongest part</i>
<i>of the human body.</i>

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:05.510
<i>The load-bearing capacity</i>
<i>of a single hair is about 150 grams.</i>

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:09.600
<i>A person has 100,000 hairs on average.</i>

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:15.900
<i>Theoretically, that means</i>
<i>a person's hair can hold 15 tons.</i>

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:19.780
<i>The Inaba Family pass all</i>
<i>their secrets on to a single child.</i>

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:24.410
<i>From childhood, he strengthens his hair</i>
<i>by rubbing a wondrous ointment into it.</i>

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:29.450
<i>The enhanced hair becomes steel wire</i>
<i>when twined, and can be used as a whip.</i>

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:32.790
<i>It's literally their one and only weapon.</i>

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.420
Yeah, all right.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:41.010
NIKO STYLE - FLAME KATA: RAGING FIRE!!

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:46.140
Were you hoping to achieve something
when you entered my space?

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.180
That isn't possible.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:50.180
And this too is impossible!

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:09.330
<i>He keeps whipping!</i>

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:12.330
<i>Ohma is having a difficult time</i>
<i>coping with the hair whipping.</i>

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:17.790
<i>It seems our bet is going to result</i>
<i>in a victory for me, Mr. Yamashita.</i>

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:23.010
<i>Is he grinning?</i>

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.880
<i>What's making him so relaxed?</i>

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:33.020
If I lose, I'll be the king of debt.

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:35.940
No!

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.350
<i>He can't breathe.</i>

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.940
<i>Now you understand, Ohma Tokita.</i>

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:46.070
<i>When it comes to pure power,</i>
<i>you are stronger than Inaba.</i>

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:47.570
<i>But...</i>

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:51.490
<i>Inaba will have you beaten before</i>
<i>you have had a chance to use your power.</i>

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:54.660
<i>He is the epitome</i>
<i>of what it is to be an assassin!</i>

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:58.580
<i>Ohma... why aren't you using "that"?</i>

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:04.050
<i>I feel like my body is being ripped apart.</i>

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:06.590
<i>This little runt.</i>

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:09.180
<i>He's quite something.</i>

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:13.970
<i>You passed!</i>

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:18.730
<i>I recognize your talent, Ryo Inaba.</i>

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:22.980
<i>Listen, Ohma.</i>

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:25.570
NIKO TOKITA
OHMA'S MASTER OF NIKO STYLE

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.950
<i>When you fight,</i>
<i>you should finish it quickly.</i>

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:30.410
<i>It's simply the easiest way.</i>

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:32.950
<i>Niko.</i>

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:36.660
<i>As I thought,</i>
<i>you and I differ on many things.</i>

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:40.830
<i>It's not fun for me at all</i>
<i>if I finish it quickly!</i>

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:44.090
I have to thank you, Ryo Inaba.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:48.550
It's been ages
since I've been this excited.

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:02.400
Come on!

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:05.530
I'll make you excited, too!

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:07.740
That's what I want.

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:22.670
HEART, STOMACH, LIVER, PANCREAS

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:25.800
<i>While losing consciousness,</i>

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.670
<i>Inaba experiences a strange sensation.</i>

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:34.300
<i>It's the opposite of the steely feeling</i>
<i>he gets while assassinating.</i>

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:37.520
<i>It's more like a burning feeling.</i>

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:44.690
<i>By training tirelessly</i>
<i>and fighting through hell,</i>

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:48.360
<i>he's devoted his whole life</i>
<i>to acquiring his skills and power.</i>

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.490
<i>None of them will work now.</i>

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:54.370
INABA STYLE: SOMERSAULT KICK

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:01.000
<i>He's incredibly strong.</i>

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:05.420
<i>Darn it.</i>

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:12.380
NIKO STYLE - REDIRECTION & FLAME KATAS

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:16.510
WILL-O'-THE-WISP

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:19.640
No...

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:21.810
<i>No, Inaba.</i>

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:26.270
<i>What happened?</i>

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:30.900
<i>I had no chance against him.</i>

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:35.700
<i>But actually, it's... not so bad.</i>

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.370
Did you have fun?

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:45.580
Ryo Inaba.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.040
The game is over.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:51.510
The winner is Ohma Tokita.

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:55.010
If you want to fight me again,
come and see me anytime.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:56.640
Welcome back.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:00.560
These ten years have felt so long to me.

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:03.680
You've finally come back!

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:05.770
<i>That day...</i>

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:09.360
<i>you threw me into the depths of despair.</i>

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:12.490
<i>But this time, finally...</i>

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:17.030
<i>I won't let anyone get in my way.</i>

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:19.370
<i>Ohma Tokita.</i>

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.210
So, Dad's pawn won.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:27.540
KENZO YAMASHITA, KAZUO'S ELDEST SON AND
THE REAL PRESIDENT OF UNDER MOUNT INC

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:28.630
Which means...

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:30.880
YAMASHITA CORPORATION

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:33.050
RAIAN KURE, UNDER MOUNT INC

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:34.420
Ohma.

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:38.050
At this rate, we're going to win
the second stage, too.

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:39.100
Okay.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:42.180
Congratulations, Mr. Yamashita.

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:45.600
Oh, Mr. Urita.

00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:50.940
I never even dreamed...
that we would fall in the first round.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:52.820
Who's this?

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:56.700
He's Mr. Urita, Ryo Inaba's employer.

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:00.410
I have this to give to you, as promised.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:02.540
<i>Oh, that's right!</i>

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:05.910
<i>I was so excited about Ohma's victory</i>
<i>that I forgot all about it.</i>

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:10.710
<i>I succeeded in obtaining a ten percent</i>
<i>share in Penasonic Corporation.</i>

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:11.840
We don't want that.

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:15.510
I don't know what you've got there,

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:18.090
but we don't care about
anything like that.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:19.590
What do you mean?

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:24.640
Ryo Inaba and I didn't fight
for stuff like that.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:29.560
We wanted to know who was stronger.
That was all.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:33.980
Don't bring that shit into our fight.

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:39.240
<i>What on earth is he saying?</i>

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:40.780
It's not just me.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.660
I know this guy thinks the same.

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:47.000
<i>How did you come to that conclusion?</i>

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:50.540
Mr. Yamashita. You really are a great man.

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:53.920
<i>How could he believe that either?</i>

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:57.630
<i>In this mood,</i>
<i>I don't even know how I feel about this.</i>

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:01.970
But you should respect
the result of the bet.

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:04.680
I beg you to take this.

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:09.310
Well, I'm not sure
what you are talking about.

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:13.650
I don't remember making a bet with you.

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:19.570
There wasn't any bet between us
in the first place.

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:24.620
We have to respect the will of
the fighters who shed their blood, right?

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:27.660
Now... we're off.

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:36.300
You have defeated me utterly,
Kazuo Yamashita.

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:38.590
What a broad-minded man.

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:41.340
<i>I am so stupid!</i>

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:44.550
<i>That was my big chance to clear my debt.</i>

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:46.600
Hey, Kazuo Yamashita.

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:49.390
Thanks.

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:54.810
<i>Okay, I know.</i>

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:59.030
<i>I can't go against him.</i>

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:36.710
<i>Inaba was...</i>

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:40.000
<i>my best friend.</i>

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:48.930
<i>I was well aware that his family,</i>
<i>the Inaba, were a clan of assassins</i>

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:52.720
<i>which had served my family,</i>
<i>the Urita, for generations.</i>

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:57.310
<i>Setting that fact aside,</i>

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:02.190
<i>I believed</i>
<i>our friendship would last forever.</i>

00:22:06.860 --> 00:22:07.780
<i>What?</i>

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:11.450
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:16.500
<i>My dad failed in his mission and died.</i>

00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:22.630
<i>I became the head</i>
<i>of the Inaba Family yesterday. And so...</i>

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:27.720
<i>as of today, you are my boss.</i>

00:22:30.260 --> 00:22:33.350
<i>I obey you, Urita.</i>

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:36.180
<i>If you command it...</i>

00:22:38.060 --> 00:22:40.060
<i>I will kill anyone.</i>

00:22:41.770 --> 00:22:42.770
<i>Don't...</i>

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:46.030
<i>Don't insult me! You </i>kombu <i>head!</i>

00:22:46.740 --> 00:22:47.740
Kombu?

00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:52.240
<i>I've never thought of you</i>
<i>as my subordinate</i>

00:22:52.740 --> 00:22:55.240
<i>or, needless to say, as a murderer!</i>

00:22:57.830 --> 00:23:03.000
<i>For so long, you've been my best friend.</i>

00:23:06.170 --> 00:23:10.340
<i>Don't say things like that to me</i>
<i>ever again, please.</i>

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:12.050
<i>I'm begging you.</i>

00:23:14.430 --> 00:23:15.510
<i>Urita...</i>

00:23:18.770 --> 00:23:19.730
<i>Sorry.</i>

00:23:28.440 --> 00:23:31.160
Where am I?

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:34.410
You're in the medical suite
in the Kengan Dome.

00:23:34.530 --> 00:23:37.620
Oh, right... I lost.

00:23:38.370 --> 00:23:41.460
Don't worry. We'll get another chance.

00:23:41.790 --> 00:23:44.790
Huh? What's happened to you, Urita?

00:23:45.170 --> 00:23:46.920
You look oddly happy.

00:23:48.170 --> 00:23:52.180
Yeah, I was just remembering the old days.

00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:55.760
Yeah? What a coincidence.

00:23:56.310 --> 00:23:59.980
I was also dreaming of the old days.

00:24:05.980 --> 00:24:06.900
PREVIEW

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:08.650
<i>Off-field brawls are also welcome!</i>

00:24:08.820 --> 00:24:10.280
<i>The gorgeous Bird of Darkness.</i>

00:24:10.400 --> 00:24:11.860
<i>A totally wacky beast.</i>

00:24:12.240 --> 00:24:13.910
<i>The legendary Genocider.</i>

00:24:14.450 --> 00:24:15.530
<i>Do you all see?</i>

00:24:15.870 --> 00:24:18.370
<i>This is the Life-or-Death Tournament.</i>

00:24:18.450 --> 00:24:19.830
<i>Next episode: "Father and Son"</i>

00:24:19.910 --> 00:24:21.500
Subtitle translation by Hinako Someno
